<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Izu Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Izu Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> covering the Izu Peninsula and the Izu Islands, now part of Shizuoka Prefecture and Tokyo. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo">Minamoto no Yoritomo</a> lived there in exile before raising his revolt in 1180. In the 1490s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-soun">Ise Moritoki</a>, later called Hojo Soun, seized Izu, the first base of the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-clan">Hojo clan</a>, and the peninsula is known for its hot springs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/izu-province.jpg" alt="Izu Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Izu.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
